# reference.in: this family's reference requirements, resolved to the exact, hashed reference.lock
# beside this file by `python -m rcp_ndcg_test.jobs.reference_lock` (owner decision 35). The tool
# constrains torch and the CUDA stack to the engine image's freeze; every other pin installs into
# the family's reference venv and takes precedence over the image's copy. Never edit the lock by hand.
# The reference environment for recipes/jina-reranker-v3/reference.py, in ITS OWN python
# (never the harness's process, never the engine image).  Install with the reference python:
# pip install -r reference.lock
# The wave runner takes that interpreter via --reference-python; the reference subprocess runs while
# the engine on that slot is up and releases its memory when it exits.
#
# Pinned to the versions the paper's [local] extra ran with (experiments/paper/rerankers/reference/
# requirements.txt): torch 2.9.1 and transformers 4.57.6.  flash-attn and accelerate are NOT needed
# here: the paper's JinaRerank loads AutoModel with dtype="auto" and default attention (sdpa).
#
#   render mode (stage 1, CPU): tokenizers + rcp-ndcg + huggingface_hub only -- no torch.
#   score mode (stage 2): everything below; downloads the 1.19 GB bf16 weights at the pinned revision.
#
# NOTE on rcp-ndcg==0.0.1: it is not yet on PyPI (the package's first release has not shipped). Until
# it is, install rcp-ndcg from the repository's build (the same commit the recipe package is checked
# out at); the pin records the release version the wave environment must match.

rcp-ndcg==0.0.1
torch>=2.9  # the paper pinned 2.9.1; the reference needs no flash-attn (sdpa) and runs on the image's torch (decision 35)
transformers==4.57.6
tokenizers>=0.22,<=0.23.0  # transformers 4.57.6 requires <=0.23.0 (the image ships 0.23.2)
numpy>=1.26
huggingface_hub>=0.34,<1.0  # transformers 4.57.6 requires <1.0 (the image ships 1.33.0)
